  "text": "Oncology in Seattle, WA  | Animal Medical Center of Seattle\nSkip to Primary Content\n24/7 Emergency\n24/7 Emergency\nCareers\nPay Online\nAbout Us\nAbout Us\nOur Team\nCareers\nNews & Events\nServices\nEmergency & Critical Care\nDiagnostic Imaging\nInternal Medicine\nInterventional Radiology\nNeurology\nOncology\nSurgery\nPet Owners\nPet Owners\nFAQs\nDocuments & Forms\nBlog\nPay Online & Payment Resources\nFor Veterinarians\nReferrals\nEvents\nResources\nrDVM Newsletter Sign Up\n24/7 Emergency\nContact Us\nOncology\nA cancer diagnosis of a pet changes you forever. The Oncology Department at Animal Medical Center of Seattle works with you to provide not only compassionate care but a wide array of advanced and effective treatment options. We will work with you and your pet and tailor each treatment protocol to allow effective cancer treatment, while minimizing major side effects.\nWhat is Interventional Oncology?\nIn human medicine, interventional radiologists routinely work intimately with oncologists to provide innovative, minimally invasive options for their patients. A similar trend has recently begun in Veterinary medicine to provide multimodal therapies along with surgeons and oncologists forming a comprehensive oncology team for our patients. Interventional oncology can help provide minimally invasive options with low morbidity for patients who have historically had limited options.\nServices Provided\nChemotherapy\nNovel therapies\nAdvanced Imaging\nSurgical consultations\nRadiation referrals\nPet loss therapy referrals\nPlease\ncontact\nour Oncology Department for more information or questions about these services.\nTypes of Cases Seen\nSpecific Types of Cancer (Malignancies)\nApocrine Gland Adenocarcinoma\nBasal Cell Carcinoma\nChondrosarcoma\nEpulis\nHemangiosarcoma\nHistiocytic Disease\nLeukemia and Lymphoma\nMelanoma\nMast Cell Tumor\nMultiple Myeloma\nOsteosarcoma\nOther – Adenocarcinoma, Carcinoma, Sarcoma, Undifferentiated\nSoft Tissue Sarcoma\nSquamous Cell Carcinoma\nThymoma\nTransitional Cell Carcinoma\nClient and Referral Forms\nYou can view the forms in PDF format by downloading the free\nAdobe Acrobat reader\n.\nOncology New Patient Form (Printable)\nOncology New Patient Form\nOncology Referral Form (Printable)\nOncology Referral Form\nOur Oncology Team\nBrittany Evans\nDVM, MS, DACVIM\nOncology\nView Profile\nBrittany Evans\nDVM, MS, DACVIM\nOncology\nView Profile\nAnimal Medical Center of Seattle\n17518 15th Ave NE\nShoreline\n,\nWA\n98155\nT:\n(206) 204-3366\nHours of Operation\nMain Hours\nMon\nOpen 24 hrs\nTue\nOpen 24 hrs\nWed\nOpen 24 hrs\nThu\nOpen 24 hrs\nFri\nOpen 24 hrs\nSat\nOpen 24 hrs\nSun\nOpen 24 hrs\n24/7 Emergency\nAbout Us\nServices\nPet Owners\nFor Veterinarians\nCareers\n©\nCopyright\n2026\nAccessibility\nTerms & Conditions\nPrivacy Policy\nPay Online\nCookie Preferences\n©\nCopyright\n2026",
